Restore the "Controller & Bluetooth Settings" main menu entry.

GuiMenu.cpp adds this entry unconditionally in the #if BATOCERA branch, but
AmberELEC builds with BATOCERA off, and in the #else branch the same addEntry
call is wrapped in a comment along with an unused "CONFIGURE INPUT" fallback -
so the entry, and everything under it (controller mapping, and the Bluetooth
pairing/device-list/toggle items gated on batocera-bluetooth existing), never
appears on any AmberELEC device.

getControllersSettingsLabel() returns a compile-time label with no dependency
on Bluetooth being present, and the Bluetooth-specific rows inside the screen
are each individually gated on ApiSystem::isScriptingSupported(BLUETOOTH), so
adding this unconditionally is exactly as safe here as it already is in the
BATOCERA branch.

--- a/es-app/src/guis/GuiMenu.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/guis/GuiMenu.cpp
@@ -269,10 +269,7 @@
 
 		addEntry(_("USER INTERFACE SETTINGS").c_str(), true, [this] { openUISettings(); }, "iconUI");
 
-		/*if (ApiSystem::getInstance()->isScriptingSupported(ApiSystem::GAMESETTINGS))
-			addEntry(GuiControllersSettings::getControllersSettingsLabel(), true, [window] { GuiControllersSettings::openControllersSettings(window); }, "iconControllers");
-		else
-			addEntry(_("CONFIGURE INPUT"), true, [this] { openConfigInput(); }, "iconControllers");*/
+		addEntry(GuiControllersSettings::getControllersSettingsLabel(), true, [window] { GuiControllersSettings::openControllersSettings(window); }, "iconControllers");
 
 		addEntry(_("SOUND SETTINGS").c_str(), true, [this] { openSoundSettings(); }, "iconSound");
 
